      "knowledge_point_id": "ce7ef1dd-58cc-57f5-9ff9-fc997f4280ee",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying True Statements Regarding an Exponential Decay Curve",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true in relation to the function $f(x)=(0.08)^{x}?$\n\nI. Its range is $y>0$\n\nII. It is an increasing function\n\nIII. $f(x)\\to 0$ as $x\\to \\infty $",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by recalling the graph of ${(0.08)}^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13941630/assets/b4e3b5119c92d02bbceb786fefd238182c7c84ca0f4abc85a19f2df86a6ba267.png)\n\nLet's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. The set of possible outputs of $f(x)={(0.08)}^{x}$ consists of all the positive numbers.\n\n- Statement II is false. For $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ falls. Therefore, $y=f(x)$ is a decreasing function.\n\n- Statement III is true. As $x$ increases, the function value gets smaller and smaller, approaching zero. Therefore $f(x)\\to 0$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and III are true.",
